# herdr writes its runtime state next to its config: session.json,
# session-history.json, herdr.sock, and the client/server logs.
#
# session-history.json is the one that matters. With [experimental]
# pane_history = true it holds recent pane scrollback in PLAIN TEXT, and
# upstream warns that pane output "can include secrets, tokens, prompts, and
# command output". It must never be committed.
#
# Today it cannot be: install.sh stows with `--no-folding`, so ~/.config/herdr
# is a REAL directory and every runtime file lands outside this repo. This
# allowlist makes that guarantee structural rather than incidental -- a
# hand-run `stow` without --no-folding would fold this directory into a
# symlink and drop all of it straight in here.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit only what is genuinely ours.
*
!.gitignore
!config.toml
!gpu-status.sh
!plugins/
!plugins/window-title-fix/
!plugins/window-title-fix/*
